From 221386a2b0eb44d596bee5da8cb248027e83c950 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 22:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 095/145] media: meson: vdec: do not announce a source change
 that did not happen

amvdec_src_change() queues a V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE unconditionally,
even down the path that has just decided the capture queue is already
configured for this stream and called codec_ops->resume() to keep
decoding with the buffers it has.

That path exists precisely because nothing userspace-visible changed, so
the event is a lie, and it is an expensive one.  Every client that
honours SOURCE_CHANGE stops its CAPTURE queue in response.  ffmpeg's
v4l2m2m decoder goes further for this driver specifically:

  // Meson (amlogic) always gives a resolution changed event after output
  // streamon and userspace must (re)allocate capture buffers and streamon
  // capture to clear the event even if the capture buffers were the right
  // size in the first place.
  if (strcmp(cap.driver, "meson-vdec") == 0)
          s->quirks |= FF_V4L2_QUIRK_REINIT_ALWAYS | ...

FF_V4L2_QUIRK_REINIT_ALWAYS forces do_source_change() to take the full
reinit branch: release every capture buffer and allocate the set again.

VP9 re-announces its frame geometry on every seek, so on a 4K profile-2
stream this fires a complete teardown and reallocation of a ~378 MB
buffer set per seek, on top of the set still in use.  Measured on a
Khadas VIM3 (896 MB CMA): playback settles at 3 MB CmaFree, the seek
releases back to 356 MB, and the reallocation then fails -

  cma: __cma_alloc_frozen: reserved: alloc failed, req-size: 2032 pages, ret: -16
  => 1100 free of 229376 total pages
  meson-vdec PRP0001:26: dma alloc of size 8323072 failed
    vb2_dc_alloc <- __vb2_queue_alloc <- vb2_core_reqbufs (VideoPlayer)

- and the session is dead: position frozen, zero decoder interrupts for
every subsequent seek.  The buffers are not leaked; CMA returns in full
on stop.  A single 4K VP9 session simply is the whole CMA budget, so
asking for a second copy of it can never succeed.

Return early once resume() has been called, as the code did before the
G12A HEVC work removed it, so a client is only told about changes that
are real.  The comment that went with it ("and do not send the event")
described the intended behaviour and is restored here.

Compare bitdepth alongside geometry and DPB size rather than assigning
it up front: bitdepth became part of this function's contract when the
10-bit support landed, and an 8->10 bit transition at constant
resolution is a genuine format change that userspace must still hear
about.

Initial negotiation is unaffected: streamon_cap is 0 until the client
has started its CAPTURE queue, so the first source change always takes
the event path.  Seeks reach here with CAPTURE still streaming because
ffmpeg's flush only stops the OUTPUT queue.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 .../staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c   | 20 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
index cc66cb111c38..af48066cd21e 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec_helpers.c
@@ -551,24 +551,30 @@ void amvdec_src_change(struct amvdec_session *sess, u32 width,
 
 	v4l2_ctrl_s_ctrl(sess->ctrl_min_buf_capture, dpb_size);
 
-	sess->bitdepth = bitdepth;
-
 	/*
-	 * Check if the capture queue is already configured well for our
-	 * usecase. If so, keep decoding with it.
+	 * If the capture queue is already configured for exactly this
+	 * stream - same geometry, same bit depth, enough buffers, still
+	 * streaming - keep decoding with it and tell userspace nothing.
+	 * Every client that honours SOURCE_CHANGE stops the CAPTURE queue
+	 * in response, and ffmpeg's v4l2m2m additionally reallocates every
+	 * capture buffer for this driver (FF_V4L2_QUIRK_REINIT_ALWAYS), so
+	 * an event for a change that did not happen costs a full 4K buffer
+	 * set each time.  VP9 re-announces its geometry on every seek.
 	 */
 	if (sess->streamon_cap &&
 	    sess->width == width &&
 	    sess->height == height &&
+	    sess->bitdepth == bitdepth &&
 	    dpb_size <= sess->num_dst_bufs) {
 		sess->fmt_out->codec_ops->resume(sess);
-	} else {
-		sess->status = STATUS_NEEDS_RESUME;
-		sess->changed_format = 0;
+		return;
 	}
 
+	sess->bitdepth = bitdepth;
 	sess->width = width;
 	sess->height = height;
+	sess->status = STATUS_NEEDS_RESUME;
+	sess->changed_format = 0;
 
 	dev_dbg(sess->core->dev, "Res. changed (%ux%u), DPB %u, bitdepth %u\n",
 		width, height, dpb_size, bitdepth);
-- 
